Z||000003||The Fieromaster||06-28-2001||05:03 PM||||If you have the side lit gauges (all pre 85 i think) to give it some X-TRA color... remove the gauges and take them apart then where it is painted orange on the back peice paint it whatever color you want (high gloss) or paint it the chrome so it reflects the color you want better!  WWorks real well!!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">    <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tweek||06-28-2001||05:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Fieromaster:<BR><B>If you have the side lit gauges (all pre 85 i think) to give it some X-TRA color... remove the gauges and take them apart then where it is painted orange on the back peice paint it whatever color you want (high gloss) or paint it the chrome so it reflects the color you want better!  WWorks real well!!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats what I did. First paint it white, hen paint the color you want, otherwise the color will be off. So far Mine went from flor. orange to met. blue (did not work at all) to flor green (did not work over the blue, came out flat) to white to flor green again. Now it works well. Still have reg. bulbs though, I'll maybe check in the using colored ones as well.||||reg||1
